{"id": "EUVD-2026-103706", "enisaUuid": "4e64bae6-b6ab-38da-b490-b22e32982f6e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: arm64: Transfer the hyp stack pages out of the host stage-2\n\nfix_host_ownership() walks only the linear-map alias of each memblock\nregion, and the per-CPU hyp stack, mapped in the private VA range for\nits guard page, has none.\n\nWalk each stack's VA range with the same walker.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:15:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:20:04", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e5dd2a91a7ae3a276e6d79806127e923936e241b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/22df195bff84300a3f04813d6148765c77ac565a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3a8c562892b96f35bba1e00d5e455a15963bbb92"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98466", "GHSA-7374-3pfm-f9q8"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "22b9199c-aad3-35de-86e9-6b1fd0f7de44", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1a919b17ef012ca0572bae759c27e5ea02bfb47f <e5dd2a91a7ae3a276e6d79806127e923936e241b"}, {"id": "54088234-2e3c-3d25-96d6-017c3dd93798", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "6751f994-d596-3bc2-ae46-e0e01d7486d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.19"}, {"id": "90a3f299-d337-35a8-8c85-bfe08c2ee53d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "944362af-dc02-3124-bf4a-6cdea95dfb11", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "9dbded8a-7696-321b-b84d-1b3c323cc296", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1a919b17ef012ca0572bae759c27e5ea02bfb47f <3a8c562892b96f35bba1e00d5e455a15963bbb92"}, {"id": "e15de61e-e426-3de9-9e97-9e5cea7b6484", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "produ